♾️ LiFT: Loop Flow Transformers 🧵👇

Diffusion models usually spend more inference compute by taking more sampling steps. What if we could also spend compute inside each step?

LiFT turns part of a DiT into a recurrent core, letting us scale depth at inference with only a small architectural change. On ImageNet, it beats dense DiT-XL/2 with 3.34 lower FID, while using 60% fewer parameters, 32% fewer training FLOPs, and 52% fewer inference FLOPs.

